{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject","id":1552366,"title":"Demon cover as a spell subject","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-14T07:06:50-07:00","id":1552366,"title":"Demon cover as a spell subject","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552365#post1552365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The example stands, in practice there's still quite a number of effects that may end up affecting the Cover rather than the Demon, depending on how the Mage defined the target (and potentially if they know the true nature of the target). It's just not the majority.<br /> <br /> But the details depend a lot on context and on how the ST interpret some things. It isn't unreasonable to think that most effects affect the Demon directly, but thinking that you need to be aware of the Demon to affect it directly isn't unreasonable, either. Further discussing it would be a topic for a whole thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, but I would wonder if most of the time Demons are unaffected by supernatural powers and fake being under their effects to avoid blowing their covers.<br /> <br /> Is that his Demon works, at least with mental powers... Like a vampire's dominate?<br /> <br /> And in the vein, how deep do covers go? If a mage attempts to directly examine the inner working of a Demon in cover, do they find memories which the demon has take from some poor human, a mind, and Oneiros? How deep does the cover go?<br /> <br /> Edit: reading through the Players guide to the Contagion Chronicle, doesn't seem to help address these questions.<br /> <br /> Assuming a Demon makes their spoof roll, a mage just gets whatever they would expect to find if there was just a person instead of a Demon, right?<br /> <br /> But only when the my have a soul pact do covers have an actual soul? This seems counter-intuitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 07-14-2025, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T08:42:23-07:00","id":1552370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject#post1552366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair, but I would wonder if most of the time Demons are unaffected by supernatural powers and fake being under their effects to avoid blowing their covers.<br /> <br /> Is that his Demon works, at least with mental powers... Like a vampire's dominate?</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, Conditions affect the demon itself as much as they do the Cover; the exception is Persistent Conditions that are part of an individual Cover, such as those representing missing limbs (see the &quot;Cover-Specific Conditions&quot; sidebar on Demon Core p80). Compromise is their incentive to allow Disquiet to affect them, but a demon affected by a mental or emotional power is subject to its effects whether they're under Cover or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And in the vein, how deep do covers go? If a mage attempts to directly examine the inner working of a Demon in cover, do they find memories which the demon has take from some poor human, a mind, and Oneiros? How deep does the cover go? </div> </div> </div>The Cover does not protect against reading the demon's mind, as evidenced by the fact that Flowers of Hell uses &quot;reduce attempts to read the user's mind about a specified event to a chance die&quot; as an example of a near-field gadget and the Storyteller's Guide's list of genre hacks for Silent games includes an Embed that specifically counteracts telepathy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But only when the my have a soul pact do covers have an actual soul? This seems counter-intuitive. </div> </div> </div>A soul pact takes an actual soul. A patchwork or angel-jacked Cover is a memetic construct that convinces the world there's a person in the space implied by the memories and material connections that support it.<br /> <br /> Spoofing is a surface baffle durable enough to persist for a scene at a time, but much as Liar's Tongue only allows them to make their statements read as true or false rather than to have scrutiny pull up an entire implied scenario, the basic function of a Cover's basic supernatural protection is to deflect casual or singular attempts to catch the Unchained out as demons \u2014 directed and prolonged scrutiny will cause it to slip eventually, especially since spoofing has no common ways to make it more likely to succeed than raising the Cover's rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T09:38:12-07:00","id":1552374,"title":"","content":"Ok so, 1) they still have an incentive to pretend to be affected by Dominate/Other mental powers which *should* affect their Cover (to avoid a compromise) right?<br /> <br /> 2) the cover has no mind of its own, so if a mage tries to mind read it, they are targeting the Mind of the Demon... <br /> <br /> 3) looking at a demon with a patchwork or angel-jacked cover and finding no soul would be a give away that there is something going on, right? or can this be spoofed for the scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T10:35:02-07:00","id":1552376,"title":"","content":"First of all, it's important to be clear that a Demon isn't less affected when the effect &quot;just&quot; affects the Cover. When it happens, the only way the Demon has to not be under the effect is to change Cover or assume demonic form. While under Cover the Demon is that person for all intents and purposes, regardless of the fact that the person isn't really human. They have the Cover's body, metabolism and social connections. The distinction isn't actually if the effect targets the Demon or the Cover, but if it relies on characteristics of the Cover the Demon don't have.<br /> <br /> Demons don't have a soul, except possibly as property. When they assume that person's life as a Cover, though, it's a Cover almost like any other. It's particularly enduring against scrutiny, but that isn't even something you can only get this way (patchwork Covers can be just as resistant once well enough established). Regardless of Cover or not, Demons don't have a Soul. While their <b>bodies</b> are essentially human, they still have more than a few actual differences from a human, and those don't cease to be because of Cover.<br /> <br /> Spoofing baffles any effect that would detect <b>that the Demon isn't human</b>. It doesn't protect the Cover at large, just the identification of inhuman traits. So yes, spoofing would fool an effect that detects souls, as it would fool any effect that directly or indirectly demonstrates that the Demon isn't an actual human being. If the effect further analyses this &quot;soul&quot;, it makes sense that it would have any characteristic expected from the Cover's soul (except that it is a normal human soul, the Cover never simulates non-human characteristics even if it was a non-human entity). If the Cover is an Angel-Jacking, Patchwork, or the original one, this soul will possibly be as unremarkable as possible, but it would still be detected despite not existing.<br /> <br /> Liar's Tongue lets the Demon pass any statement as true or false, as they please. IF a supernatural scrutiny just examines the veracity of what they say, they can fool the effect without a roll. But any other effect that would read the mind of the Demon does read their actual mind. Reading a mind isn't affected at all, except in the very strict sense of detecting the intention to lie or not. Then the mind reader may find out the Demon isn't Human (or at least don't think to be so) through the contents of their minds, although that would reasonably require a lot of probing, as you can't just pick this precise information (and probably doesn't have a reason to try).<br /> <br /> By the way, <b>this is a Compromise</b>. The Demon makes a Compromise Roll every time someone finds out they're not their Cover, or at least strong evidence in this direction.<br /> <br /> It's also relevant for the mind reading that Demon directly states that the Demon doesn't learn any memories of their target when making or cashing in a Pact, they are encouraged to learn about the life of their target beforehand. A Demon that doesn't does a good job is even prone to end up causing Compromise without knowing why. On the other hand, Demons spend a lot of time living as their Covers. Even if they don't regard themselves as that person (which many don't, but also many do), it's probable that most of their thoughts are perfectly reasonable for that person. A Demon is likely to have perfectly mundane thoughts about a lot of perfectly mundane things they do every day.<br /> <br /> Now, if the Demon should pretend to be affected by something or not to avoid Compromise... it depends. At the end of the day, Compromise depends on a lot of things. Sometimes people can be remarkable resistant to a power, either by high Attributes or dumb luck, so resisting isn't necessarily a Compromise. The user of the power would have to have a very, <b>very</b> good reason to think it not working is something to suspect. And of course, if the witnesses already know the Demon isn't Human, then there's no Compromise: it only happens when the information gleaned is new to the person learning it. And it doesn't depend on the &quot;size&quot; of the discovery. A Demon being harassed by someone investigating them may even straight up tell the truth to that person and make a Compromise Roll, simply because that way they don't have to make any other Compromise Roll because of this person, ever again (although if this person tells others, that's a problem).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T11:00:34-07:00","id":1552378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552376#post1552376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;snip&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that detailed responce.<br /> <br /> Two things occur to me. Having no soul doesn't indicate a person isn't human, lots of human may have no soul (depending on who is going around eating souls). <br /> <br /> So I could be happy to leave mages with some demons having souls (the covers from Soul Pacts) and some not... (But you'd have to explain over time why they don't degenerate.<br /> <br /> I had assumed that reading a Demon's mind would immediately out them as *not* human, as their minds must be completely different. They just don't work of think like humans, even if they may find themselves thinking more like a human the more they live in one cover.<br /> <br /> That said, spoofing should protect against this. But if it only makes it look like a human mind, and is still the Demon's thoughts (a Demon's mind filtered through the spoof of how a human would think these thoughts?) then this problem is avoided - while not making it any more difficult for either the mind reader or the demon..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T11:19:20-07:00","id":1552379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552374#post1552374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) looking at a demon with a patchwork or angel-jacked cover and finding no soul would be a give away that there is something going on, right? or can this be spoofed for the scene?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, looking for a soul in a demon will return no soul, but looking for a soul in a regular human whose soul has been stolen will also return no soul.<br /> <br /> <i>No</i> demons have souls. A soul pact <i>requires </i>a soul to make and cash in, but the process of cashing it in and claiming the Cover involves annihilating the original human, soul included.<br /> <br /> I would not assume that reading a demon's mind would produce a structure by which you could intrinsically discern a demon from a human, any more than reading a werewolf's mind or a vampire's mind. They have thoughts and feelings. Now, their mind can do <i>unexpected things</i> which may draw suspicion. They might be thinking about what they want to do as a different person from their current Cover. Or they might use the Liar's Tongue to alter the truth valence of what they believe: a demon can freely alter the outcome of any attempt to discern what the demon genuinely believes to be true. But you don't pick up &quot;quantum brain interaction&quot; from the demon deciding in the moment that they don't believe the sun exists, you just pick up &quot;this guy doesn't believe the sun exists.&quot;<br /> <br /> Spoofing only works against effects that specifically discern whether you are a supernatural being or not. It would work on the Supernal Vision spell, for example. It wouldn't work to disguise whether a demon has a soul or is thinking about doing something a human can't do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T11:41:33-07:00","id":1552381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552374#post1552374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so, 1) they still have an incentive to pretend to be affected by Dominate/Other mental powers which *should* affect their Cover (to avoid a compromise) right?</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>are</i> affected by other mental powers. Disquiet affects them normally but allows them to not act on it at the cost of compromise because Disquiet does not narratively compel action and being in demonic form allows them to ignore Disquiet without further risk of exposure. There is no such out for supernatural powers directly applied via a resisted or contested roll. Demons with functional knowledge of Medicine can bootstrap a desired emotional response in themselves for mechanical purposes, but that's not going to let them ignore or Clash with a magical power that makes them act or feel a certain way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) the cover has no mind of its own, so if a mage tries to mind read it, they are targeting the Mind of the Demon... </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) looking at a demon with a patchwork or angel-jacked cover and finding no soul would be a give away that there is something going on, right? or can this be spoofed for the scene? </div> </div> </div>Soul Marks detects soullessness through the presence of the Soulless Persistent Condition and its derivatives. If the demon fails to spoof the spell, it would also detect that they are a supernatural being. Death Sight would not necessarily register the Cover as having a soul, but as addressed above, that doesn't automatically out them as nonhuman and the fact that ordinary humans have souls means spoofing would probably still falsify the basic presence of a soul.<br /> <br /> Weird Virtues and Vices showing up to Know Nature might trip flags, but a) mages occupy a setting where magic can change a person's Anchor Traits, b) demons can, with a little effort, learn to channel different Virtues and Vices for different Covers, and c) even the quirks of their origins leading to different Virtues and Vices for demons doesn't change the fact that living as humans means their thought processes are functionally human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T19:12:30-07:00","id":1552396,"title":"","content":"One thing to understand is that ultimately Spoofing and other Demon abilities is meant to be overpowered against cursory observation, despite not really protecting against a focused, persistent probing. Demons not only aren't especially resistant to careful analysis, they're actually particularly vulnerable to even completely mundane investigations, <i>as long as those are focused and persistent</i>.<br /> <br /> But again, within a cursory observation Spoofing should <i>always</i> win out when it activates correctly. Since the Demon doesn't suffer from the Soulless Condition, it should be assumed as default that Spoofing simulates a soul, and <b>nothing</b> inherent to the soul should give it away promptly. Under a cursory observation, even if it is soul analysis magic, this soul is unremarkable. Anything about the Demon is unremarkable at a cursory glance if it would give away that they're not Human.<br /> <br /> As a concept, the idea is to avoid suspicion, not to fool an investigation. What happens is that while most supernaturals, and in fact many people, could find out the Demon if they really try, <i>the Demon doesn't give them a reason to</i>, at least not easily. If someone is using an effect of any kind and nature to look at several people at once, looking for the person that stands out as suspiciously inhuman, the Demon that successfully Spoofs should <i><b>always</b></i> read as perfectly normal. Their actions, not their nature, is what can draw attention.<br /> <br /> So a &quot;Soulless&quot; Demon is, indeed, perfectly possible, but shouldn't be taken as default. If there's a reason for the Cover to be under Soulless, then a Cover may start to read as having no soul, but that isn't a common thing to happen. In fact, it's possible in theory for a Cover to <b>have</b>, indeed, this Condition, and then the Demon doesn't just behave as if they had it, they <b>actually do</b>. But such a Cover would also be hard to come by (I'm not sure, but I think that even for a minor Pact the person has to have a soul, so this can't be constructed as a Patchwork Cover. It would have to be an Angel-Jacking Cover designed with Soulless by the God-Machine).<br /> <br /> What can easily draw attention from a Mage, though, is if they use a spell to affect the Demon's soul in some way. Because the spell will fail, and it will fail for lack of a target. Spoofing may make it look like the Demon just resisted the spell, but it can only go so far. That's again the point where Demons don't have much against a more careful analysis. It's even theoretically possible that upon being targeted by a spell that removes their soul, the Demon acquires Soulless for the Cover, yet the Mage doesn't get any soul out of them. This would be a quite contrived situation, but stands as an example of how the rules work.<br /> <br /> Mind-wise, Demons don't have particularly inhuman thought processes. Quite the opposite, more than many other splats Demon is pretty clear that they have quite human-like minds, even though they aren't human at all (and many have no interest in seeing themselves as human). Most of the reasons for the Fall are quite human thoughts or emotions. Demons have complete control of their body's response, being able to pretend or conceal emotions without need for a roll, but the mind behind the facade does in fact feel like any human being and will make decisions based on those emotions like anyone else. It isn't uncommon for the emotion mimicked by the Demon to actually be completely real.<br /> <br /> Demons usually live most of their lives as their Covers, whether they like it or not. They eat, drink, defecate, work, go to shitty family reunions, have mundane friends, coworkers and romantic relationships. While <i>sometimes</i> their interest in those relationships is fake (a lot of times it isn't), they are still just as real and mundane as it seems. Yes, you can read the mind of a Demon at the moment they're thinking about a heist against Infrastructure, or about changing Covers. But you can just as easily, and possibly even more probably, read it when they're thinking about the new hire at the company, or which grocery they'll go to, or the hours they're planning to spend painting miniatures. Demons tend to spend more time in mundane activities than most other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T20:32:26-07:00","id":1552398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552396#post1552396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure, but I think that even for a minor Pact the person has to have a soul, so this can't be constructed as a Patchwork Cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanics just say that you can't sign a soul pact if you're Soulless and that only mundane parts of one's life can be offered as Cover, albeit those mundane parts can include &quot;owns a (potentially mystical or supernatural) object noteworthy enough to be associated with them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T21:36:35-07:00","id":1552399,"title":"","content":"Then it isn't possible to Patchwork Soullessness, but just because it isn't mundane. So it stands, the only option (to have Soulless as a Demon) would be the highly unlikely occurrence of Angel-Jacking a Soulless Cover so designed by the God-Machine. Or, by the way, to have your own first Cover to be that Cover (your first one is always designed by the God-Machine).<br /> <br /> And keeping in mind that even if a Patchwork Cover can't be supernatural in its description, a Soul Pact can be signed with any supernatural creature that does have a soul, and I guess a Deviant counts. Such Cover is a hard one to fill, because while the Cover is completely human by definition, it doesn't change that its identity isn't. A Remade Cover would still be hunted by conspiracies, a Vampire Cover would have a position in the All Night Society and so on.<br /> <br /> In those cases, the lack of their actual supernatural powers can not only lead to problems galore, but it can cause unavoidable Compromise, as the Demon is physically incapable of actions expected from the Cover, and Spoof still only makes the Demon appear human, not the Cover's supernatural species. This makes supernatural Covers pretty rare as they're very hard to maintain and hardly pay off, although they're not particularly hard to get (far easier than getting Soulless).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T21:56:42-07:00","id":1552400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552399#post1552399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it isn't possible to Patchwork Soullessness, but just because it isn't mundane. So it stands, the only option (to have Soulless as a Demon) would be the highly unlikely occurrence of Angel-Jacking a Soulless Cover so designed by the God-Machine. Or, by the way, to have your own first Cover to be that Cover (your first one is always designed by the God-Machine).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the soul from a Cover made from a soul pact being stolen using Sever the Awakened Soul, per the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle, which, of course, is still not the same as a Cover that was never a whole legitimate human life having the Soulless Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T00:03:49-07:00","id":1552403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552400#post1552400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the soul from a Cover made from a soul pact being stolen using Sever the Awakened Soul, per the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle, which, of course, is still not the same as a Cover that was never a whole legitimate human life having the Soulless Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't keep a soul from a soul pact, it gets annihilated when you cash the pact in and claim the Cover. There is no soul to steal once the Cover belongs to the demon, and Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed's sidebar on how soul stealing spells interact with other splats affirms that it doesn't work on the Unchained.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle says one or two things that are just wrong, or at least, contradicted by/incompatible with the other books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T06:02:35-07:00","id":1552410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552403#post1552403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle says one or two things that are just wrong, or at least, contradicted by/incompatible with the other books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon itself contradicts the established information about how souls work \u2014 most notably with the Raise Dead Exploit not working properly in its normal use case \u2014 and the text on what calling in a soul pact itself does both largely uses the language it does to mean &quot;the person you're replacing isn't coming back&quot; and then immediately introduces a speculative workaround that is trivial for player characters to test. I don't feel anything particularly breaks from saying that a Cover created via a soul pact annihilates the material body and personality of the pactbound and gives the demon calling it in a more consistently durable identical Cover with the pactbound's soul for the purposes of crossover with the splat whose soul-handling tools are the most diverse of the main eleven and who treats individual souls as mostly fungible save for effects that require a character to have their own soul.<br /> <br /> The information the PGCC introduces establishes the thematically consistent notion that Kindred vampires and Unchained demons as a whole have access to limited abilities to handle souls without the need to develop extra powers to do so. Vampires destroying each other's stolen souls through diablerie is consistent with the consumptive nature of vampirism and the worst effects of diablerie on the diablerist are not incompatible with the destruction of a type of soul that conventionally shouldn't still be around; demons take souls through a type of documentation that largely negates its effects when destroyed, use them to produce Covers that reflect the subject's former breaking points (and, with practice, Anchors), and already use another related mechanic to functionally replace objects with near identical copies that possess supernatural powers derived from the God-Machine. On the opposite end of things, the PGCC <i>is</i> consistent with N&amp;A about the Begotten not having souls that can be affected by Awakened soul-manipulation despite both of those being contradicted by Beast Core, so in the interest of not getting too caught up in the weeds I'm inclined to defer to the newer material, particularly since one of the writers of the PGCC was the creator and co-developer of Demon.<br /> <br /> &quot;Demons don't have souls and annihilate the people they replace when they use their innate ability to subvert a person's place in the world through their soul&quot; is not especially contradicted by &quot;Covers created by 'taking' a pactbound soul narratively still have the soul, which requires a degree of Death magic to remove that only the Moros, a member of a Death-focused Legacy, or a Tremere with Hollow 7+ can achieve without a teacher,&quot; because the demon is still a being that does not have its own soul that can be stolen outside of that Cover identity. You could alternatively speculate that calling in a soul pact is the equivalent of using the destruction of a soul as a sacrament for a spell to create a Destiny, but considering the most predictable consequences of destroying a soul pact includes &quot;the demon loses the Cover and takes damage from the destruction of a permanent pact&quot; either way and the rest of the extended mechanics for Cover include &quot;people and things whose relationships with you are enshrined parts of your Cover damage it when they die or are destroyed&quot; I feel it's more interesting to minimize the amount of functionally dead pact documentation on an Unchained character sheet in a context where they're interacting with mages capable of interacting with souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T06:09:11-07:00","id":1552412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552410#post1552410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires destroying each other's stolen souls through diablerie is consistent with the consumptive nature of vampirism and the worst effects of diablerie on the diablerist are not incompatible with the destruction of a type of soul that conventionally shouldn't still be around</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should vampire souls not be around?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T06:53:21-07:00","id":1552413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552412#post1552412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should vampire souls not be around?</div> </div> </div> </div>The soul vanishes completely at the moment of death and yet Kindred can be Embraced as much as a week later (with the process of arising taking up to six more nights to finish in that case) and even outside the context of the posthumous Embrace the normal process is described as feeding a corpse or a person who has died. By the metaphysics of the soul that Mage explicitly uses, a vampire should not have a soul in a sense that can be interacted with normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T10:41:09-07:00","id":1552419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552413#post1552413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yet Kindred can be Embraced as much as a week later (with the process of arising taking up to six more nights to finish in that case)</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I do think some of this raises a question to examine in gameplay of whether or not the souls of the atypically Embraced vampire are identical to that of the conventional one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">even outside the context of the posthumous Embrace the normal process is described as feeding a corpse or a person who has died. By the metaphysics of the soul that Mage explicitly uses, a vampire should not have a soul in a sense that can be interacted with normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do acknowledge that your phrasing probably conveys a point that it's part of the mystery of vampirism as to why they have souls under such circumstances, but I think even apart from that it's looking at a few things a bit strictly. &quot;Moment of death&quot; is a bit of a vague description, after all. I would also propose that, given the significance of humanity to vampires, there's a basis to extrapolate backwards from the fact that they do have souls after having died to an idea that there can be a bit more going on in the process of the Embrace than just what is conveyed by the infusion of Vitae.<br /> <br /> (I'm also recalling how some people have taken a bit of an issue with phrasing that implies that people revived from medical death might be rendered soulless)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T12:27:19-07:00","id":1552422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552419#post1552419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I do think some of this raises a question to examine in gameplay of whether or not the souls of the atypically Embraced vampire are identical to that of the conventional one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Functionally they're the same as typically-Embraced Kindred, which suggests any differences would be more esoteric than just the means of their initiation into the Requiem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do acknowledge that your phrasing probably conveys a point that it's part of the mystery of vampirism as to why they have souls under such circumstances, but I think even apart from that it's looking at a few things a bit strictly. &quot;Moment of death&quot; is a bit of a vague description, after all. I would also propose that, given the significance of humanity to vampires, there's a basis to extrapolate backwards from the fact that they do have souls after having died to an idea that there can be a bit more going on in the process of the Embrace than just what is conveyed by the infusion of Vitae. </div> </div> </div>Humanity is lost from the sire when creating a vampire who isn't a dead end for their lineage, but while revenants cannot create more revenants they <i>do</i> start with the same amount of Humanity as a fresh fully-Embraced Kindred and the conventional means of their arising operate on a similarly delayed timetable to that of the posthumous Embrace, i.e. as much as a week postmortem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (I'm also recalling how some people have taken a bit of an issue with phrasing that implies that people revived from medical death might be rendered soulless) </div> </div> </div>While it's generally out of the scope of ChroD's damage mechanics to model, I nevertheless get the distinct impression clinical death and a full Health track of aggravated damage are separate things for the purposes of metaphysics for this very reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T18:51:00-07:00","id":1552471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552422#post1552422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Humanity is lost from the sire when creating a vampire who isn't a dead end for their lineage, but while revenants cannot create more revenants they <i>do</i> start with the same amount of Humanity as a fresh fully-Embraced Kindred and the conventional means of their arising operate on a similarly delayed timetable to that of the posthumous Embrace, i.e. as much as a week postmortem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well my meaning in using the lower case h there was to convey that I'm not talking about Humanity the mechanic so much as the underlying premise of why it is called that.<br /> <br /> The subtext that I take from Requiem Second Edition is &quot;vampires are actually still a lot more human than they want to acknowledge&quot;. To whit, I would find significance in taking the mechanics given for how soul manipulating magic works with them to mean that their human souls are actually pretty much intact, or at least retained in a new context.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T20:33:16-07:00","id":1552473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552471#post1552471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To whit, I would find significance in taking the mechanics given for how soul manipulating magic works with them to mean that their human souls are actually pretty much intact, or at least retained in a new context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is getting a bit afield of the fact that in normal circumstances the soul departs at the moment of death and becoming a vampire of the sort we're talking about requires you to die.<br /> <br /> The arguable least complicated explanation for Requiem-style vampires having souls that can be affected by Awakened magic is that the taint of vampirism (whether by consumption of Vitae or being exsanguinated by a vampire) allows the Embrace to retrieve it from whatever its destination would have been as much as a week later.<br /> <br /> It could alternately be the case that the Embrace produces something that serves as a functional replacement for a normal human soul that is metaphysically different, but whatever the details of the process, a vampire's soul has some degree of connection with the metaphysical qualities Kindred accord to the Beast \u2014 Tremere can use stolen vampire souls to project a Predatory Aura \u2014 and people who have died aren't supposed to still have their souls under normal circumstances, to the point where Geist 2e apparently had bits rewritten before its Kickstarter to account for the geist taking the place of the soul instead of merging with/attaching to it.<br /> <br /> Mage's own spell for resurrection specifies that soul loss sets in on the newly-revived subject no matter how long they've been dead, the version of the Embrace with the shortest timeframe of execution still requires the prospective vampire be exsanguinated (which, assuming a generous reading of &quot;dead&quot; and/or a direct transference of a statement in the Requiem 1e corebook into an edition where being fully dead is no obstacle to performing the Embrace, leaves them with minutes to live at best), and the nature of torpor and the daysleep mean from the start of their Requiem a Kindred is familiar with the sensation of returning to consciousness from death.<br /> <br /> Bringing it back around to the point of this tangent, vampires' ability to interact with souls is limited to tainting their owners to be valid subjects for the process to make more vampires and consuming the souls of their fellow vampires for rewards that are largely fungible and based around the thematic notion that the Blood tends to bleed qualities together, so &quot;consuming a soul destroys it and leaves the vampire who ate it with distracting remnants of its owner's personality&quot; doesn't imply that demons, whose ability to interact with souls is limited to seizing ownership of them through a written agreement as the token of their ability to assume their appearance and socially-accorded possessions and connections, necessarily destroy the soul in the course of hijacking its place in the world any more than a soulless mage who uses a Hung Spell to capture the soul of a victim they murder at the moment of death implies that the soul is destroyed it its integration into the mage.<br /> <br /> Compartmentalization is a key point of Demon's personal metaphysics and the splat's general lack of other published soul-handling tools mean the only functional distinction for the Unchained is that using a soul-pacted Cover to go loud might be considered a greater loss than it would for other types of Cover (potential capacity to spawn an Echo notwithstanding), so there's not much thematic or mechanical basis for the oldest gameline in the Revised Storytelling System to insist upon the material repossession of a soul making it irretrievably gone when the splat has a &quot;destroy an entire human life&quot; mechanic that can be used on a Cover regardless of its provenance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T22:14:54-07:00","id":1552474,"title":"","content":"To me it's a question less of the technicalities and more of the thematic underpinnings. I think it's thematically significant for vampires to still have at least partially human souls. I think it's thematically significant for the Unbound to have nothing of the sort. I find the metaphysical backfilling should proceed from that.<br /> <br /> One thing I would extrapolate is in my comment about a bit more going on with the Embrace. Kind of a notion that a killing under circumstances where an Embrace is imminent might hold a soul in place to await how it plays out. Some subtle operation of how the aura of a vampire applies itself, akin to the effect their long term residence has on the mood of a place, or how the Cacophony perpetuates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T04:12:13-07:00","id":1552482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552474#post1552474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it's a question less of the technicalities and more of the thematic underpinnings. I think it's thematically significant for vampires to still have at least partially human souls. I think it's thematically significant for the Unbound to have nothing of the sort. I find the metaphysical backfilling should proceed from that.<br /> <br /> One thing I would extrapolate is in my comment about a bit more going on with the Embrace. Kind of a notion that a killing under circumstances where an Embrace is imminent might hold a soul in place to await how it plays out. Some subtle operation of how the aura of a vampire applies itself, akin to the effect their long term residence has on the mood of a place, or how the Cacophony perpetuates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm with you thematically.<br /> <br /> For Mage, the game is about mysteries, and what happens to soul is definitely one.<br /> Observig what happens when a person is embraced may be dubiously ethical, but these are mages.<br /> <br /> Given the claims made by the Strix and the mechanics by which they can replicate, and given the cost associated with embrace, it think it is possible that a small amount of the site gets transferred into the victim/childe. In which case, a new Strix-like entity is created from the old. And it fill the place of the soul (with the Beast qualities as mentioned previously...) but maybe that only happens for some clans, and maybe it still happens but has nothing to do with the Strix it is just the animating force of kindred is something which takes up the space that a soul would be, and a Mage could try studying it.<br /> <br /> Not sure how this relates to Demon covers, but it is an interesting point of conversation.<br /> <br /> For Vampire, it doesn't really matter.<br /> <br /> For Demon, I guess the only case it matters is when they soul pact a Vampire... But you would want to be a very careless vampire to give your entire soul to a demon...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T06:12:00-07:00","id":1552483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552474#post1552474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it's a question less of the technicalities and more of the thematic underpinnings. I think it's thematically significant for vampires to still have at least partially human souls. I think it's thematically significant for the Unbound to have nothing of the sort. I find the metaphysical backfilling should proceed from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile, the metaphysical backfilling i'm proceeding from includes &quot;Demon and Mage both approach the soul as peripheral to the ability of a personlike actor to act like a person and inhabit a place in social-metaphysical reality&quot; and &quot;Covers made with human souls are more durable against investigation as a fundamental quality rather than as it pertains to those aspects that were present when the demon acquired them&quot; and &quot;Covers can have Persistent Conditions attached to them rather than the demon itself, of which Soulless is one.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, it's not really significant in Vampire that they have humanlike souls, either, except as extra spice on the consequences of diablerie as a form of turbo-murder, because the only soul-tampering power in the corebook that doesn't also annihilate the target doesn't work on monsters. Likewise, in their own game it's largely immaterial to the Unchained whether calling in a soul pact destroys the soul along with the unfortunate pactbound's body and mind or simply binds it to the demon, because they can still trade the Cover to other demons, the demon itself still doesn't have the soul in a mechanical sense nor suffer from the effects of soul loss outside of that Cover if it's removed, and getting a Cover that has had its soul removed is an extreme corner-case due to the requirement that the signatory of a soul pact have their soul at the time of signing.<br /> <br /> Mage doesn't treat the game-mechanical soul as having the thematic function vampires are riffing on when they talk about maladies of the soul (even Promethean uses those issues as shorthand for &quot;making a soul is extremely difficult and the Created do so by learning about humanity from the outside), and as far as the matter of interactions between two different splats that mess with souls in a fungibility-oriented way the technicality <i>is</i> the bigger question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T11:55:33-08:00","id":1557349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1552410#post1552410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the text on what calling in a soul pact itself does both largely uses the language it does to mean &quot;the person you're replacing isn't coming back&quot; and then immediately introduces a speculative workaround that is trivial for player characters to test.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to raise the topic from the dead, but I thought y'all were having a very interesting discussion. I would note that the PGCC also flat-out says that demons and vampires <i>do </i>have souls, though you all might have covered that. <br /> <br /> <i>Flowers of Hell </i>also attempts to give any sort of &quot;this isn't the most evil thing you can possibly do&quot; spin to soul pacts, for probably the same reason that speculative workaround was included. Soul pacts are monstrous. I think it probably should have been more difficult to reverse a cashed-in soul pact, along the lines of the contract being burned up or something, but yeah. <br /> <br /> Fun stuff, y'all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T00:02:56-08:00","id":1557579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1557349#post1557349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Flowers of Hell </i>also attempts to give any sort of &quot;this isn't the most evil thing you can possibly do&quot; spin to soul pacts, for probably the same reason that speculative workaround was included. Soul pacts are monstrous. I think it probably should have been more difficult to reverse a cashed-in soul pact, along the lines of the contract being burned up or something, but yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you may be missing is that &quot;soul&quot; in the game has a very specific and <i><b><u>counter-intuitive</u></b></i> meaning. It is <b>not</b> what we usually understand as a soul.<br /> <br /> Most characters talk about souls in a more coloquial way, like vampires talking about <i>Diablerie</i>. For those, we have to keep in mind that <i>they don't know what a soul is</i>, just as we don't IRL. You may have all your personal beliefs about souls, but there are many ways to define and understand them, and zero ways to verify any of them. When talking about souls, those characters are talking about particular phenomenon they experience that they <i>interpret</i> as pertaining to the soul. But they have no means to test it.<br /> <br /> Some splats, like Demon and Mage, have access to the <i>mechanical soul</i>. But that's not necessarily what <i>we</i> would call a soul, and it's just as impossible to verify on this regard as absolutely any other concept of soul. The <i>mechanical soul</i> is an entity (in the broadest sense possible) that's common to all humans and affects some aspects of their mental health and behavior. It's a fungible entity, which means that to date no meaningful distinction was ever found between regular souls. You can transplant souls from one person to another and that won't transplant absolutely no known property of the donor, no diseases, no virtues, no vices, no personality quirks, no nothing, which goes against usual definitions of soul and is a very good indication that the game is <b>not</b> talking about &quot;actual souls&quot; (as far as they can be defined) when talking about <i>mechanical souls</i>.<br /> <br /> That's it about souls when Demon talks about soul pacts. It looks terrible, until you get that no one actually have any idea of what that <i>thing</i> being called a &quot;soul&quot; is, beyond that a living human need one (any one) to be healthy. For all we know it may be little different from asking for someone's kidney. No one knows what happens to a person upon death. No one knows what role this piece has after death. We know upon a person's death it vanishes to who-knows-where if not magically preserved. We know ghosts are not made of this stuff and are not really the living person, just an echo. We know it may have distinct properties for supernatural &quot;humanoids&quot;, and that people without one are still essentially the same person. And we only know stuff about it to the degree that people in the setting can interact with the stuff through powers, which means everything beyond strict empirical observation is speculative at best.<br /> <br /> I don't know if upon death you'll need your heart, as a piece of your soul, for the gods to weight it and decide your fate. It may be that extracting someone's heart is condemning them for eternity. But I can't say a transplant doctor is committing &quot;the most evil thing you can possibly do&quot; if this is not something the doctor knows about or believes in. So no, reaping <i>mechanical souls</i> through pacts is not it, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T00:13:49-08:00","id":1557580,"title":"","content":"I think the thing that might make people regard the soul pacts of the Unchained as morally dubious at best isn't so much what it means to their speculative afterlife or identity or anything else to do with the absence of a soul so much as the fact that calling one in deletes a person from existence to allow the Demon to assume their identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T06:07:58-08:00","id":1557593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1557579#post1557579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some splats, like Demon and Mage, have access to the <i>mechanical soul</i>. But that's not necessarily what <i>we</i> would call a soul, and it's just as impossible to verify on this regard as absolutely any other concept of soul. The <i>mechanical soul</i> is an entity (in the broadest sense possible) that's common to all humans and affects some aspects of their mental health and behavior. It's a fungible entity, which means that to date no meaningful distinction was ever found between regular souls. You can transplant souls from one person to another and that won't transplant absolutely no known property of the donor, no diseases, no virtues, no vices, no personality quirks, no nothing, which goes against usual definitions of soul and is a very good indication that the game is <b>not</b> talking about &quot;actual souls&quot; (as far as they can be defined) when talking about <i>mechanical souls</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you describe as the Mechanical Soul, may just be in part of the Five-fold soul, as described by Mummy.<br /> <br /> Indeed, soul loss as described in Mage results in a hollow shell of a person, barely able to decide to defend themselves, never mind get out of bed and eat...<br /> <br /> But Mage also talks about the Onerios as a kind of inner reflection of the soul. Allowing them access what is potentially a seperate part of the Five-fold soul. From there you can disconnect vices or virtue and personality quirks and integrate them into other people (with the right magics...).<br /> <br /> Arguable a person's Destiny is another aspect of their soul, which can be transferred.<br /> <br /> Demon can take all of these things, afaik, not just personality traits, they can build a cover from your socially connections, your resources, your destiny, everything that makes a person can be negotiated away. <br /> <br /> Nevermind the mechanical Soul. That seems to be necessary to empower humans, to give them the drive to act on their identity (and yes, that is fungible). But Demons can steal much more than just that - infsctt, if I'm not mistaken, Demons don't really need the mechanical soul, and it is unclear is a Mage (even with Mastery of Death) could steal the soul from a demon's cover ....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T10:02:13-08:00","id":1557604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1557580#post1557580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the thing that might make people regard the soul pacts of the Unchained as morally dubious at best isn't so much what it means to their speculative afterlife or identity or anything else to do with the absence of a soul so much as the fact that calling one in deletes a person from existence to allow the Demon to assume their identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's this. You aren't just killing someone by taking their metaphysical kidney; you're utterly annihilating them from the universe, as far as we know, to take their place. Death wouldn't be so bad. Even stealing someone's soul is less horrific, in some ways, <i>because it's still there</i>. What we're talking about is something far more heinous. Demons know what they're doing, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T17:58:09-08:00","id":1557626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552366-demon-cover-as-a-spell-subject?p=1557604#post1557604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it's this. You aren't just killing someone by taking their metaphysical kidney; you're utterly annihilating them from the universe, as far as we know, to take their place. Death wouldn't be so bad. Even stealing someone's soul is less horrific, in some ways, <i>because it's still there</i>. What we're talking about is something far more heinous. Demons know what they're doing, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do know it may be possible that something of them is released Sheen the cover gets burnt. If only because the God-Machine has recruited that something (and presumably transformed it) to use against the Demon which destroyed it. <br /> <br /> There is an one example of an Echo which is on the ghost spectrum, but enhanced in various ways by the G-M, and the only example we have is rank 4... which is pretty strong compared to a normal ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T21:08:54-08:00","id":1557699,"title":"","content":"Yes. There are some small possibilities that might allow for the soul's return, but they're apocryphal at best. To be honest, I'd have liked another crack at how some of this works, but as it stands, the soul pacts are exceedingly horrific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}